Dear Soheil, Thank you very much for your detailed reply and for answering
all of my questions so openly. I truly appreciate your professionalism and
the time you have taken to provide such detailed information. It has been a
pleasure getting to know more about Raspina Clothing and your approach to
working with international customers. Thank you as well for explaining your
production process. It is very helpful to understand how you organize
manufacturing and cooperate with partner factories while maintaining your
quality standards. As part of my work, I always carry out a due diligence
review before introducing a manufacturer to potential customers. This helps
me better understand the company and confidently present it to my business
partners. I hope you don't mind if I ask a few more questions. Could you
please share: =E2=80=A2 Your Business Registration Certificate (or Company
Registration Certificate); =E2=80=A2 Your company registration number; =E2=
=80=A2 Your
export license (if applicable); =E2=80=A2 The legal name of the company exa=
ctly as
it appears on the registration documents. I would also be grateful if you
could clarify one more point. In your company presentation, you mention
woven fabric production, circular knitting production, and warp knitting
production. Could you please explain whether these facilities belong to
Raspina or to your manufacturing partners? This information will help me
better understand your production structure and present your company
accurately to potential customers. There is absolutely no rush. I
understand that collecting these documents may take some time. Thank you
once again for your openness and professional communication. I look forward
to hearing from you. Best regards, Chulpan


